## Public Directory Structure

```plaintext
public/
├── favicon.ico
├── logo.svg
├── manifest.json
├── robots.txt
├── preview-image.png
├── invoice-template/
├── receipt-template/
├── icons/
└── assets/
```

---

## Folder Purpose

The **public/** directory contains static assets required for TWO’s deployment, branding consistency, application previews, downloadable templates, and browser-level configuration.

These files support the product’s visual identity and production readiness.

---

# File Breakdown

## favicon.ico

Purpose:

Browser tab identity for TWO.

Used for:

- Browser tabs
- Bookmarks
- Saved shortcuts

Design requirement:

Should reflect TWO’s minimalist fintech branding.

---

## logo.svg

Purpose:

Primary scalable brand logo.

Used across:

- Authentication screens
- Dashboard navigation
- Landing page
- PDF invoice exports
- Receipt templates

Requirements:

- Lightweight
- Vector-based
- Responsive
- High clarity at all sizes

---

## manifest.json

Purpose:

Defines Progressive Web App configuration.

Supports:

- Mobile installability
- App icon behavior
- Device launch experience

Configuration includes:

- App name
- Short name
- Theme colors
- Background color
- Display mode

---

## robots.txt

Purpose:

Controls search engine crawling behavior.

Supports:

- Deployment indexing
- Search discoverability

---

## preview-image.png

Purpose:

Social sharing preview image.

Used for:

- GitHub repository preview
- Deployment previews
- Social media sharing cards

Design requirements:

Should showcase:

- TWO branding
- Dashboard preview
- Product tagline

---

# invoice-template/

Contains reusable invoice export templates.

Examples:

- Default invoice layout
- Branded invoice variations
- PDF rendering templates

Purpose:

Ensures consistent invoice generation.

---

# receipt-template/

Contains receipt export templates.

Examples:

- Standard receipt layout
- Compact receipt format
- Printable receipt version

Purpose:

Supports instant invoice-to-receipt conversion.

---

# icons/

Contains application iconography.

Examples:

- Dashboard icons
- Navigation icons
- Status indicators
- Action icons

Purpose:

Maintain interface consistency.

---

# assets/

Contains additional static resources.

Examples:

- Illustrations
- Empty-state graphics
- Onboarding visuals
- Landing page visuals

Purpose:

Enhance visual communication.

---

# Public Asset Design Principles

All static assets must follow:

## Brand Consistency

Align with TWO’s visual system.

---

## Performance Optimization

Assets must be:

- Lightweight
- Compressed
- Fast-loading

---

## Scalability

Assets should remain sharp across:

- Mobile
- Tablet
- Desktop
- High-resolution displays

---

## Accessibility

Visual assets should:

- Support sufficient contrast
- Avoid ambiguity
- Improve comprehension

